    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch12-19: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.23";
    dc:description "Existing neuroscience data may test local predictability but cannot resolve the claimed origin of apparent freedom. Every plausible observation remains compatible with several rival mechanisms, making the central explanatory claim non-discriminating.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: A proxy study could compare predictability of neural dynamics with reported agency, but no agreed measurement maps apparent freedom to computational irreducibility or separates this explanation from chaos, noise, and incomplete observation.";
